 {"id":"AUG-073","title":"[P2] CONTRIBUTING's contributor verification loop is wrong on 3 axes: points at substrate-bound smoke.sh instead of the substrate-free gate.sh, declares 8 of 13 verbs as 'the API', and no machine-readable version exists anywhere","priority":"P2","complexity":2,"status":"pending","created_at":"2026-09-25 02:16:38","updated_at":"2026-09-25 02:16:38","reasoning":"PM lane sweep 2026-09-25 (premises verified live, not hunter claims): (1) CONTRIBUTING.md 'Run the smoke test' is the ONLY pre-PR check it names, and tests/smoke.sh hard-requires a live DuckBrain+JEV substrate; tests/gate.sh — the script CI actually runs on every push/PR (ci.yml comment lines 3-12, AUGER_CI guard) — is never mentioned, so a substrate-less contributor has no documented pre-PR check. (2) CONTRIBUTING 'The verbs are the API' lists init,start,ask,answer,check,status,toggle,dump but the real top-level surface is 13 verbs (auger --help): bundle, propagate, feedback, recall, verdict are uncovered by the breaking-change contract. (3) No __version__ in auger.py, no --version flag, no CHANGELOG.md, no pyproject.toml: 'v0.1' exists only as README prose, bug reports have no version to quote, future tags have no in-code anchor. Related but distinct from RELEASE-001 (tags/releases exist nowhere) and AUG-039 (README token claim) — this row is the contributor-docs + version-string axis. Pass criteria: CONTRIBUTING names tests/gate.sh as the substrate-free pre-PR check (CI runs it with live arms skipped); the API-stability contract covers all 13 verbs matching --help, with a rule that adding a verb updates the list; python3 auger.py --version (or AUGER_VERSION) prints a version whose single source lives in auger.py; CHANGELOG.md exists with a v0.1 entry.","detail":{"fingerprint":"c43de1ace435dc34d7fac2983ced21ff81ed731f5481857b15af8455af120ee2"}}
 {"id":"AUG-074","title":"[P1] init hardcodes ~/duckbrain/namespaces for declaration files and exits 0 on a 0/14 tally — a non-default substrate namespaces path yields a green init that breaks at start","priority":"P1","complexity":2,"status":"complete","created_at":"2026-09-25 10:55:00","updated_at":"2026-09-26 15:10:00","reasoning":"Dogfood run 8 (failure-semantics leg). ns_dir() (auger.py:318) is os.path.expanduser('~/duckbrain/namespaces/<ns>') — hardcoded, while the substrate honors DUCKBRAIN_NAMESPACES_PATH (run 8 used a scratch substrate on :3121 with namespaces under /tmp). Live result: init wrote the 14 declaration files into the PRODUCTION tree on the control host and printed 'declared: 0/14 tables' plus a WARNING listing all 14 as 'not visible to the API yet' — then exited 0; start then died with \"insert project failed (404): Table 'project' not found\". VERBS.md's init contract says the declared tally is how the count is checked, but a 0/14 tally still exits 0. A user following the README's own DUCKBRAIN_DATA_DIR fresh-install advice plus a non-default namespaces path gets a broken install with a green-looking init. Fix direction: (a) resolve the declaration directory from the substrate's configured namespaces path (registry entry from GET /api/namespaces or an env passthrough), not from ~; (b) exit non-zero (or refuse) when the tally is 0/14 on a create/init run. Minor same-family friction: 'start -p <id>' silently ignores -p (minted P-20260925103605 despite the flag); an ignored-flag hint would save a round-trip.","completed_at":"2026-09-26 15:10:00","commit_hash":"2a6056a","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","foreman_note":"Steward close (tick auger-2026-09-26-19-34-37) of the stranded lifecycle from tick auger-2026-09-26-13-40-24 (audit event 155 promised row close follows the verdict; the tick died first). Fix 2a6056a landed 2026-09-25 23:34 (init resolves DUCKBRAIN_NAMESPACES_PATH and refuses a 0/N declared tally). Live legs verified foreman