 {"id":"AUG-075","title":"[P1] check and recall FAIL OPEN on a dead substrate: rc=0 'no stored evidence matched — treat as a new question' / empty recall while the store is unreachable","priority":"P1","complexity":2,"status":"complete","created_at":"2026-09-25 10:55:00","updated_at":"2026-09-25T19:45:00Z","reasoning":"Dogfood run 8: killed the substrate (kill -9) and probed every verb. status/dump/ask/answer/feedback/verdict all fail CLOSED — rc=1, \"transport: Connection refused\", <1s, nothing hangs, nothing invented. But check returned rc=0 with 'no stored evidence matched — treat as a new question' while D-001 (a decision closing exactly that question, verified intact after restart) sat in the unreachable store, and recall returned rc=0 with an empty result set. VERBS.md's honesty contract ('a refused write exits non-zero and says why'; check 'never writes anything', and drifted records must not be silently misreported) is upheld for writes and broken for the two retrieval verbs: 'we hold nothing' is reported when the truth is 'we cannot reach what we hold'. A user trusts the false negative and re-drills an answered decision. Fix direction: distinguish empty-answer-set (200, 0 rows) from transport failure in the db_select/db_retrieve callers of check and recall, and fail closed (rc=1, 'substrate unreachable') exactly as write verbs already do — two call sites. PM 09-25: fix landed in 715be71 (09-25 08:03, SubstrateError fail-closed across check/recall/ask/gate_question + docs/VERBS.md). Evidence: pytest 3 fail-closed cases (test_recall_transport_failure_is_a_failure_not_an_empty_store, test_check_fails_closed_when_the_substrate_is_dead, test_gate_question_reports_a_dead_substrate_as_an_error) = 3 passed 0.03s. Closed by PM lane, verified live.","commit_hash":"715be71"}
